# The bar wandering
# The bar's one and only movement: end to end, back and forth, forever. Times are
# estimates - time one full traverse and correct this file.

0 The bar sets off towards one end of its travel, sliding steadily. It uses its whole length, not a small sway.
30 It takes roughly half a minute to cross from one end to the other.
0 It arrives, and immediately sets off back the other way without pausing.
30 The return crossing takes the same time.
0 And so on, indefinitely, at the same speed and over the same full length.
0 On the way it passes the meeting points where a male sits directly in front of a female. There are six such points; five of them lie within the bar's travel, so the bar passes them on every crossing. Male 2 in front of female 3 lies just past the end of the travel, so that pair is never brought together by a wandering bar - only by a person driving the bar there from the control page.
0 Nothing aims the bar. It does not know which male is calling, which female is looking, or where the meeting points are. Any encounter you witness happened because the bar's wandering and a female's turning coincided by chance.
